# Copy to .env and adjust. Both the API server and the Vite dev server read this file.
#   Linux / macOS:  cp .env.example .env
#   Windows:        copy .env.example .env
# Every line is optional: without a .env, add your folders in the app under Settings.

# Folders scanned for PDFs on first start (only used while no folder is configured yet;
# afterwards manage folders in the app under Settings).
# Separate several with ":" on Linux/macOS and ";" on Windows.
#   Linux:   STUDYSPACE_LIBRARY_DIRS=/home/you/University/Semester
#   macOS:   STUDYSPACE_LIBRARY_DIRS=/Users/you/University/Semester
#   Windows: STUDYSPACE_LIBRARY_DIRS=D:\University\Semester
STUDYSPACE_LIBRARY_DIRS=
# Comma-separated folders or files to hide, e.g. Old, *.md (the same rules as in Settings).
STUDYSPACE_EXCLUDES=

# Where the SQLite database, your notes' pictures and edit backups live. Defaults:
#   Linux:   ~/.local/share/studyspace
#   macOS:   ~/Library/Application Support/StudySpace
#   Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\StudySpace
# STUDYSPACE_DATA_DIR=

# API server address (the web UI proxies /api to it). 127.0.0.1 = this computer only;
# 0.0.0.0 = also your phone on the same Wi-Fi (it must log in with the password below).
# STUDYSPACE_HOST=127.0.0.1
# STUDYSPACE_PORT=4317
# The web page's port with `npm run dev` (if it is taken, the next free one is used and printed).
# STUDYSPACE_WEB_PORT=5173

# Lets other devices (a phone over Wi-Fi or Tailscale) log in. Without it, only this computer
# can use StudySpace. This computer itself never needs it.
# STUDYSPACE_PASSWORD=
# Extra host names other devices may use, comma-separated (this computer's IPs, its name,
# localhost and *.ts.net always work).
# STUDYSPACE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# Undoable file edits kept per PDF (page edits / Save to PDF). Each keeps the previous file
# version under <data dir>/history. 0 disables undo for file edits.
# STUDYSPACE_HISTORY_LIMIT=10

# OCR (optional, runs only when you use the OCR tools). How to install: REQUIREMENTS.md.
#   Ubuntu/Debian: sudo apt install ocrmypdf tesseract-ocr     macOS: brew install ocrmypdf
# Languages: install e.g. tesseract-ocr-ben and set STUDYSPACE_OCR_LANG=eng+ben.
# Programs that aren't on the PATH can be given with their full path.
# STUDYSPACE_OCR_LANG=eng
# STUDYSPACE_OCRMYPDF=ocrmypdf
# STUDYSPACE_TESSERACT=tesseract

# Slides (.pptx, .ppt) are turned into a PDF by LibreOffice the first time they are opened.
# Empty: look for soffice, then libreoffice, on the PATH, then in the usual install folder
# (C:\Program Files\LibreOffice on Windows, /Applications on macOS).
# A snap LibreOffice can't see /tmp or ~/.local, so it works in
# ~/snap/libreoffice/common/studyspace unless STUDYSPACE_CONVERT_DIR is set.
# STUDYSPACE_SOFFICE=libreoffice
# STUDYSPACE_CONVERT_DIR=

# Files deleted in the library go to a Trash folder you can restore from. Defaults:
#   Linux: the desktop Trash (~/.local/share/Trash).  Windows / macOS: <data dir>/Trash.
# STUDYSPACE_TRASH_DIR=

# Optional AI provider. "none" keeps StudySpace fully offline. See docs/DEVELOPER.md.
AI_PROVIDER=none
# AI_API_KEY=
# AI_MODEL=
# AI_BASE_URL=
